      <h1>Hermione — DannStarr</h1>
      <p>Hermione is Dan Starr’s privately operated AI assistant, running on Hermes Agent. This page describes the Google Workspace connection operated by Dan for his own accounts and DannStarr Electronics business administration. It is not a public sign-up service or a RepairKeeper customer integration.</p>
      <h2>What the connection does</h2>
      <p>With the account owner’s explicit consent, the connection can access Gmail, Google Calendar, Drive, Docs, Sheets and read-only Contacts. These capabilities support understanding correspondence, preparing Gmail drafts, organising appointments, finding relevant files and assisting with documents and spreadsheets.</p>
      <p>Connecting an account does not itself activate inbox monitoring or automatic replies. Sending messages, changing appointments, editing or sharing documents, and other consequential actions require the owner’s instructions or a separately agreed, bounded automation policy.</p>
      <h2>Private access, not public data</h2>
      <p>Google account data is accessed through authorised APIs. Relevant information may be processed by external AI services to fulfil requested tasks; it is not automatically published on this website. There is no Google sign-in or upload form on this page.</p>
      <p>Read the <a href="/hermione/privacy/">Hermione Google connection privacy policy</a> for details of data access, processing, storage and revocation.</p>
      <h2>Operator and support</h2>
      <p>Operated by Dan Starr, trading as DannStarr Electronics, United Kingdom. For connection support or privacy enquiries, contact <a href="mailto:dannstarrelectronics@gmail.com">dannstarrelectronics@gmail.com</a>.</p>
      <p><a href="/">Return to TechFath3r</a></p>
    </Prose>
